lines=['# scan: six closed sources and33-kernel phase decomposition','', '**Finding:** CH and DH both obtain substantial F128/F256 speedups. Most benefit is shared system improvement; F128 slightly reduces DTC relative advantage, while F256 adds only a small relative improvement. F256 CH/DH speedups are1.272539/1.283635 and I=1.008719. Same-F CH/DH=1.018102, favoring DH modestly. This is one frozen input, not a selected-suite GM.','', 'All six sources are naturally closed accepted results; both new CH runs passed an independent frozen read-only strict/true164/native-restore audit. No live input or controller observation was consumed as performance, no new model was launched, and no original identity, source, budget, registry, controller, owner or manuscript was changed.','', '## Identity and actual33-kernel contract','', 'Full digest `6df3a84b612086e8c10f7f66978b6b995b459a38b00892152cf116e90db72e39`. Actual ordered full-body qualification and strict/raw stats:33kernels,1,963,460,720retired active-thread instructions and166,608CTAs. Each kernel\'s own grid/block/name/instruction count is verified, including fresh bounded4096-byte header reads. There are17LocalScan,8Partials and8UniformUpdate launches, not11identical triplets: the initial10LocalScan captures have the same grid/block but differing instruction counts, followed by the actual remaining partial/update/local sequence. No native full-application or capture ELF/numeric completeness is newly certified.','', 'Fixed Core `9eedb3131937748f0492fa83aad37d3691118d70`, Framework `02775fd795cde5aae1480d81cee6eb481d0a08f4`, binary SHA `02a289360b42a573832698c978f21ad2125182a453067a35be60410f1eb8888d`. Original CH-P0/DH-P0/DH-F128/DH-F256 are exact original-index full-digest/cell/profile matches, including disclosed inherited aliases. New CH roles remain STAGEII_AUTHORIZED_CH. No R2/IR/EP/PQPS replacement occurs.','', '## Matched performance','',tab(['Profile','CH cycles','DH cycles','S_CH','S_DH','CH_F/DH_F','I=S_DH/S_CH'],[[p,by['CH',p]['cycles'],by['DH',p]['cycles'],1 if p=='P0'else next(x['S_CH']for x in d['matched_performance']if x['profile']==p),1 if p=='P0'else next(x['S_DH']for x in d['matched_performance']if x['profile']==p),by['CH',p]['cycles']/by['DH',p]['cycles'],1 if p=='P0'else next(x['I']for x in d['matched_performance']if x['profile']==p)]for p in['P0','F128','F256']]),'', 'F128 CH gains17.8254% in reciprocal-cycle speed versus DH15.6693%, yielding I0.981700 and DH0.9253% more cycles than CH. F256 CH gains27.2539% versus DH28.3635%, yielding I1.008719. Do not describe the28.36% DH self-speedup as28.36% improvement relative to CH: the relative increment is0.8719%. No per-program best-F choice is used to create a unified GM.','', '## Every captured kernel: actual shape/instructions/cycles','', 'Symbols are actual trace/strict names. Phase labels are fixed source candidate mappings: LocalScan=`scanExclusiveShared`, Partials=`scanExclusiveShared2`, UniformUpdate=`uniformUpdate`. Source mapping is conditional, while kernel identity/order/shape/instruction/cycles below are trace/runtime evidence.','',tab(['K','Kernel symbol','Candidate phase','Grid/block','Instructions','CTAs',*[c+'-'+p for c,p in pairs]],[[g['ordinal'],g['kernel'],g['source_phase_candidate'],str(g['grid'])+'/'+str(g['block']),g['instructions'],g['complete_CTA'],*[by[c,p]['kernels'][g['ordinal']-1]['cycles']for c,p in pairs]]for g in geo]),'',tab(['SUM','Instructions','CTAs',*[c+'-'+p for c,p in pairs]],[['All33',sum(g['instructions']for g in geo),sum(g['complete_CTA']for g in geo),*[sum(k['cycles']for k in by[c,p]['kernels'])for c,p in pairs]]]),'', 'All33cycle sums exactly equal their accepted whole-replay cycles. Different LocalScan instruction counts and the initial sequence are preserved; no aggregation substitutes an assumed repeated triplet.','', '## Phase cycle contributions','',tab(['Candidate phase','Launches','Instructions',*[c+'-'+p for c,p in pairs]],[[phase,gby['CH','P0',phase]['launches'],gby['CH','P0',phase]['instructions'],*[gby[c,p,phase]['cycles']for c,p in pairs]]for phase in phases]),'',tab(['Design','Variant','Phase','Cycle delta vs P0','Share of total saved cycles %'],[[c,p,phase,gby[c,p,phase]['cycles']-gby[c,'P0',phase]['cycles'],100*(gby[c,'P0',phase]['cycles']-gby[c,p,phase]['cycles'])/(by[c,'P0']['cycles']-by[c,p]['cycles'])]for c in['CH','DH']for p in['F128','F256']for phase in phases]),'', 'F256 CH saves1,437,258cycles: LocalScan1,049,420, Partials1,154, UniformUpdate386,684. DH saves1,469,176: LocalScan1,038,753, Partials1,122, UniformUpdate429,301. LocalScan and UniformUpdate dominate both designs\' gains; partial-sum stages are a very small contributor. DH F128 Partials slightly regress by4cycles and remain present. These shares are arithmetic decomposition of measured cycles, not causal attribution to a particular counter.','', '## Traffic and retry evidence with explicit endpoints','', 'L2 GLOBAL accepted/miss counts are32-byte sectors; accepted excludes retry events and misses=MISS+SECTOR_MISS. DRAM data values are issued32-byte atoms across20controllers. All-L2 retries and ICNT blocked admission are events, not occupancy or critical-path stall time. The final additive stream0snapshot covers all33kernels and is not added to earlier cumulative snapshots.','',tab(['Counter',*[c+'-'+p for c,p in pairs]],[[name,*[by[c,p]['totals'].get(k)for c,p in pairs]]for k,name in keys]),'', 'Whole-replay DRAM read and write volumes are nearly unchanged across profiles, despite sizable cycle improvement. F128 can improve runtime while visible retry/admission events rise in a design; F256 changes retry composition rather than eliminating all pressure. Traffic volume alone is insufficient to explain speedup.','', 'Phase-class table below sums only explicit completed-kernel print-interval differences, never cumulative snapshots. Every selected field has both endpoints and sums back to final totals (111CPU checks include endpoint conservation). An interval may contain a response to an earlier kernel\'s request, so these are print-interval event groups, not guaranteed request-origin attribution. Missing endpoints would remain null; means/gauges/peaks are never differenced.','',tab(['Source','Candidate phase','L2 GLOBAL accepted','GLOBAL misses','DRAM reads32B','DRAM writes32B','All-L2 retries','ICNT admission events'],[[g['cell']+'-'+g['profile'],g['candidate_source_phase'],*[g['print_interval_additive_sum'].get(k)for k,_ in keys]]for g in sorted(groups,key=lambda g:(g['cell'],g['profile'],phases.index(g['candidate_source_phase'])))]),'']
