lines+=[tab(['Selected cumulative reason',*[c+'-'+p for c,p in pairs]],[[k,*[by[c,p]['raw_reason_final_explicitly_printed'].get(k)for c,p in pairs]]for k in reasonkeys]),'', 'Read MISS_QUEUE_FULL generally falls at F256, while entry-capacity failures rise sharply (CH3,094,450 ->38,005,512; DH3,084,447 ->39,630,061). Entry and existing-address merge-list failures are distinct retry causes; neither is a queue occupancy measurement or critical-path time. Missing positive-only reasons remain MISSING, never automatically0. A change in retries does not establish the cause of the cycle savings or guarantee a benefit from more entries.','', '## Source and measurement boundaries','', 'Atlas47a097aad4406893a07f8d230e1e0a850609bf39 maps fixed source candidates to local scans (`scan.cu:49-153`), chunk-total scan (`156-181`) and uniform offset updates (`185-201`;launch240-310). These routines have different access/dependency/reuse opportunities. FIXED_SOURCE_PHASE_MAPPING.json retains source commit/report SHA and exact mapping; source-to-capture ELF/numeric linkage remains unresolved. Static address overlap is not a measured cache hit, MSHR merge or exact runtime concurrency.','', 'CH active PAPER_BASE common PIB256 and DH PAPER_OO PIB128 remain separate active paths; generic DH PIB8 is inactive for OO admission. OO PIB-full/Tag-conflict events remain unprinted/null, not CH zeros. Cross-design L1/Tag/physical pool/queue/timing/area differences remain disclosed. Whole-replay finite-service sample/entry ratios are in TYPED_ACTIVE_PATH_COUNTERS.json; they are not critical-path durations and do not erase burst/per-SM bottleneck possibilities.','',tab(['Source','Reported mflatency','Reported ICNT-to-memory','Reported ICNT-to-shader','Reported MRQ'],[[c+'-'+p,*[by[c,p]['strict_latency_counters'].get(k)for k in['averagemflatency','avg_icnt2mem_latency','avg_icnt2sh_latency','avg_mrq_latency']]]for c,p in pairs]),'', 'The final strict metrics/mean dictionary has mixed scopes; a last printed mean is not automatically the last-kernel mean or exact whole-application mean. Known500,000cycle sample/print/update-tail limits remain. MRQ has a distinct cumulative request denominator, not a complete L2-to-DRAM or critical-load service interval. CH MRQ188 ->346 ->614 and DH184 ->337 ->628 rise while runtimes improve. No kernel mean is summed/differenced or filled with0 when missing.','', 'Within each design only FR-FCFS size64/128/256 changes, with coupled memory-partition shared-credit limits255/319/447 (return queue192, two subpartitions, private1each). DRAM850MHz, Core/ICNT/L2 clocks,10MiB L2 capacity/mapping and each design\'s frontend remain fixed. This is window plus credit expansion, not a pure isolated queue-capacity or equal-area hardware result.','', 'Facts: both designs accelerate, principally in LocalScan/UniformUpdate, with nearly fixed DRAM traffic and only a small F256 relative DH increment. Association: changing scheduling/credits and visible admission/retry mix coincides with faster completion. Mechanism remains a hypothesis: queue/credit occupancy, bank service, request age and dependency-critical paths are not captured by these aggregates. No new experiment, controller action, remaining48batch or paper modification is performed.','', '## Reproduction and source locator','', 'Run `python3 analyze_three_profiles.py`, `python3 validate_and_group.py`, `python3 render_scan_report.py` to regenerate this new packet only. ACTUAL_INPUT_AND_KERNEL_CONTRACT.json and ACTUAL_33_KERNEL_GEOMETRY.json retain each input/member SHA, exact ordered symbol/shape/instruction/CTA. SIX_CLOSED_SOURCE_DATA.json preserves all RESULT/raw/exit SHA, UUIDs/roles/aliases/options, six-field per-kernel additive intervals, explicit retry reasons and separate means/gauges/peaks. PHASE_GROUPS.json sums only legal interval values. Both new CH independent strict/archive/native-restore receipts are retained.','',f"CPU_VALIDATION.json: {v['count']}checks PASS; six closed sources, two newCH archive audits, zero live points consumed, zero model/control actions. Root alone publishes.",'',tab(['Source','RESULT path','RESULT SHA256','UUID','Raw gzip SHA256'],[[c+'-'+p,by[c,p]['RESULT_path'],by[c,p]['RESULT_sha256'],by[c,p]['uuid'],by[c,p]['raw_gzip_sha256']]for c,p in pairs]),'']
